-- title:
--   Lemma 6, p. 18 — the cost increment Δ_n(Alg) = RNF′(r_n) − RNF(r_n) upon a new job is at most its new dual variable α′_n
-- statement:
--   At the arrival of job $n$ at time $s=r_n$, the alive jobs $A$ (released no later than $s$, with positive residual lengths $\rho_j$) form the identical-release instance $\mathrm{RNF}(r_n)$. Adding job $n$ with its length $v_n$ gives $\mathrm{RNF}'(r_n)$ (Definition 3). Let $(\alpha',\beta')$ be an optimal solution of the dual (2) of $\mathrm{RNF}'(r_n)$; Algorithm 2 sets the dual variable of job $n$ to $\alpha'_n$. Then the cost increment of Definition 4 satisfies
--   $$\Delta_n(\mathrm{Alg})=\mathrm{RNF}'(r_n)-\mathrm{RNF}(r_n)\;\le\;\alpha'_n .$$
--
--   In the proof of Theorem 3 this bounds each arrival's cost increment by the dual objective increment (22).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The inequality is stated as $\mathrm{RNF}'\le\mathrm{RNF}+\alpha'_n$ in $[0,\infty]$, with $\alpha'_n=a'_nv_n$ in per-unit variables. This is equivalent because $\mathrm{RNF}$ is finite.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--
--   - generalization: α′_n the dual variable generated by Algorithm 2 → a′_k v_k for every optimal dual (a′, β′) of RNF′(r_n); reason: Algorithm 2 takes an optimal dual of RNF′(r_n) (p. 15), so the generated one is covered
--   - generalization: the instance RNF(r_n)/RNF′(r_n) met by Algorithm 2 at the arrival of job n (alive jobs A(r_n), residual lengths) → every identical-release instance GFCS(s) of jobs A with r_j ≤ s and positive lengths ρ_j, plus a new job k with r_k = s and length v_k; reason: every arrival of Algorithm 2 is such an instance (A = A(r_n), ρ = residual lengths), so the statement specializes to the paper's
--   - encoding: RNF′(r_n) − RNF(r_n) ≤ α′_n → rnf (insert k A) ≤ rnf A + ofReal(a′_k v_k) in ℝ≥0∞; reason: equivalent since RNF is finite; avoids truncated subtraction in ℝ≥0∞
--   - encoding: dual (2): α_j/v_j ≤ β_t + g_j(t) for all t ≥ r_j, α_j, β_t ≥ 0 → per-unit variables a_j = α_j/v_j (residual length for GFCS(s)); β integrable on the horizon; β ≥ 0 and the constraints hold for almost every t; reason: β is a density on the time axis: changing it on a null set changes no dual objective; the pointwise form would make optimal duals ill-defined
-- source:
--   Etesami, An Optimal Control Framework for Online Job Scheduling with General Cost Functions, arXiv:1906.02644v3, p. 18, Lemma 6 (with Definition 3, p. 15, and Definition 4, p. 18)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_GenCostSched_GFCS_Model

open MeasureTheory Set
open scoped ENNReal

namespace GenCostSched.GFCS

/-- Lemma 6 (p. 18): when job `k` (released at `s = r_k`, length `v_k`) is added to the
identical-release instance of the alive jobs `A`, the increase `Δ = RNF′ − RNF` of the optimal
value is at most `α′_k = a′_k v_k`, for every optimal dual `(a′, β′)` of `RNF′`. -/
theorem lemma_6 {m : ℕ} (I : Instance m) (hI : ∀ j, I.JobStanding j) (s : ℝ)
    (A : Finset (Fin m)) (ρ : Fin m → ℝ) (k : Fin m) (hk : k ∉ A) (hA : ∀ j ∈ A, I.r j ≤ s)
    (hrk : I.r k = s) (hρ : ∀ j ∈ A, 0 < ρ j) (hρk : ρ k = I.v k)
    (a' : Fin m → ℝ) (β' : ℝ → ℝ) (hopt : IsOffOptDual I.g s (insert k A) ρ a' β') :
    rnf I.g s (insert k A) ρ ≤ rnf I.g s A ρ + ENNReal.ofReal (a' k * I.v k) := by sorry

end GenCostSched.GFCS
